    "body": "Reject duplicate release messages for already-terminal transfers in _handle_release_message (matching the existing guard in _handle_remote_blocks_message). This prevents unbounded ACK object creation from repeated releases targeting the same transfer_id.\n\nAdd TTL (30s) and capacity (1024 entries) bounds to _pending_unmapped_acks in the producer get_finished path. ACKs whose transfer_id is never mapped (e.g. from rejected requests that never reach update_state_after_alloc) are now evicted instead of accumulating indefinitely and being rescanned every scheduler tick.\n\n<!-- codex-pr-hygiene-validation -->\n## Rebase validation — 2026-10-27\n\nRebased onto upstream main, preserving the original fix and current surrounding behavior. The duplicate audit found no complete merged or open replacement for this PR’s remaining control.\n\nValidation on macOS CPU: **38 passed, 3 skipped**. All applicable changed-file pre-commit checks and `git diff --check` passed.\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu VLLM_PLUGINS='' PYTHONPATH=. HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_moriio_tp_ack.py tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_moriio_kv_layout.py -k 'ack or release' -q --tb=short -p no:cacheprovider\n```\n\nNative GPU/RDMA execution and model evaluations were not run during this rebase; required CI and human review remain pending. AI assistance (OpenAI Codex) was used for the conflict resolution and validation.\n",
